6521840,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4jjjNw","name":"resterm_Linux_x86_64.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":87,"digest":"sha256:5bfe5818d692bd248269c4acf9795b2fd5a831b597f499d330bb5eef18754a0f","download_count":1,"created_at":"2026-09-28T22:04:18Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T22:04:18Z"},{"id":596521853,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4jjjN9","name":"resterm_Windows_arm64.exe","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":64453632,"digest":"sha256:c744029eb8a977cb36f56b656ee8d03c12e9f0fe77cc8b3cc288964ca2079bbf","download_count":3,"created_at":"2026-09-28T22:04:18Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T22:04:20Z"},{"id":596521846,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4jjjN2","name":"resterm_Windows_arm64.exe.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":92,"digest":"sha256:a99016c6b64f4d4276bbacbbc660d86ef51034131281eba1cd9c5d06e29a796d","download_count":20,"created_at":"2026-09-28T22:04:18Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T22:04:18Z"},{"id":596521844,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4jjjN0","name":"resterm_Windows_x86_64.exe","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":69248512,"digest":"sha256:976ea7e94c0bee556288d0da1f42ee618e2a68cbc88fd02585d79867adab239c","download_count":6,"created_at":"2026-09-28T22:04:18Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T22:04:22Z"},{"id":596521842,"node_id":"RA_kwDOP5rK3s4jjjNy","name":"resterm_Windows_x86_64.exe.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":93,"digest":"sha256:86f1ee35a76a50771897be33a2084d4d3006664e87331ddc9aef4fb5b5e85195","download_count":20,"created_at":"2026-09-28T22:04:18Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T22:04:18Z"}],"body":"## v1.10.1\r\n\r\nThis patch changes how a named command auth is defined. In 1.10.0, a word after `@auth <scope file|global> file command` became the definition's name, so a request file written for 1.9.1 could lose its default auth without an error, like `@auth file command gh`. A definition is now named with `name=`.\r\n\r\nIf you have not updated yet, see the [1.10.0 release notes](https://github.com/unkn0wn-root/resterm/releases/tag/v1.10.0) for `cmd=`, named command auth, errors for options with spaces around `=`, and the Headers tab.\r\n\r\n## Named definitions use name=\r\n\r\n```http\r\n# @auth global command name=gh cmd=\"gh auth token\"\r\n\r\n### User\r\n# @auth use=gh\r\nGET https://api.github.com/user\r\n```\r\n\r\n- `name=` can go anywhere on the line.\r\n- Only `command` definitions on `@auth file` and `@auth global` lines take a name. A request line with `name=` is an error.\r\n\r\nIn 1.9.1, a word after `command` was ignored, so this line was the default for every request in the workspace:\r\n\r\n```http\r\n# @auth global command gh argv=[\"gh\",\"auth\",\"token\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn 1.10.0, `gh` became the name of the definition. Named definitions are not inherited, so requests that relied on the line were sent without auth. Now the line is an error:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nerror[parse]: @auth expects key=value options but got \"gh\". Write name=gh to name a definition\r\n--> defs.http:1:3\r\n     |\r\n   1 | # @auth global command gh argv=[\"gh\",\"auth\",\"token\"]\r\n     |   ^\r\n```\r\n\r\nRequests that take their auth from the line fail with the same error instead of being sent:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nerror[auth]: @auth expects key=value options but got \"gh\". Write name=gh to name a definition (/work/api/defs.http:1)\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo fix the line, do one of these:\r\n\r\n- Remove the word to keep the line as the default, as it was in 1.9.1.\r\n- Write `name=gh` to make it a named definition, and add `# @auth use=gh` to each request that needs the token.\r\n\r\n## Completion\r\n\r\n- `@auth` suggestions follow the line. After `@auth file`, only auth kinds are offered. After `command`, only command options. After `use=gh`, only `header`, `scheme`, and `timeout`.\r\n- On a `file` or `global` line, choosing `command` leaves the options open and suggests `name=` first. On a request line it still inserts `cmd=\"gh auth token\"`.\r\n- `use=` suggests definitions from every file Resterm scans. In 1.10.0 it only suggested names from the open file. The same applies to `@apply use=`, `@ssh use=`, and `@k8s use=`.\r\n- A global definition in a subdirectory is suggested only when Resterm runs with `-R`, the same as when a request runs.\r\n\r\n## Changed\r\n\r\nThese changes may affect existing request files:\r\n\r\n- A word after `@auth file command` or `@auth global command` is an error. Write `name=<some_auth_name>` for a named definition, or remove the word.\r\n- A definition written for 1.10.0, such as `@auth global command gh cmd=\"gh auth token\"`, needs `name=gh`. Until then, the line reports the error above, and requests with `@auth use=gh` fail with `@auth use=\"gh\" not found`."}
